WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.760
We ask a lot of questions
about our diet.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.080
What’s the right way to
treat a chronic illness?

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.720
Fight off a virus,
lose weight?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.640
The problem is, we get
a lot of different answers.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.920
Well, I’m here to help.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.040
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.560
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.413
Today, in part three of
our series on Ozempic,

00:00:22.413 --> 00:00:26.621
we look at how to control the
side effects of GLP-1 drugs.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.080
It appears the vast majority
of people prescribed GLP-1 drugs

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.640
stop taking them
in a matter of months.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.160
But compare that
to older weight loss drugs.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.340
Those had a 98 percent
failure rate.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:39.280
As I’ve mentioned,
in drug trials,

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.400
most people taking
these types of weight-loss drugs

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.800
started out obese
and ended up obese

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.680
no matter how long
they stayed on them,

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:47.240
but that’s just on average.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.920
Some people, despite being
on high-dose Ozempic for years,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.400
actually ended up heavier
than when they started,

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.440
and most remained overweight,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.760
but a small fraction of them,
about 1 in 25,

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.720
plateaued down
at a normal weight.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.680
One in 25
doesn’t sound like a lot,

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.000
but obese individuals
are rarely able

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.800
to achieve a normal weight.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.400
Without something drastic,
like bariatric surgery,

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.960
only about 1 in 200 men
with class 1 obesity,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.520
or 1 in 100 women,

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.360
are able to find their way back
to a normal weight;

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.400
so, these drugs
really can have a huge effect

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.120
on a select few.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.680
Of course, you’d presumably
have to stay on them forever

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.160
to maintain that weight loss

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.360
at a cost of maybe $16,000
a year.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.840
But even for those
who can afford the cost,

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.760
the main reason
they stop taking GLP-1 drugs

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:38.120
is the gastrointestinal
side-effect profile.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.640
The most common side effects
of Ozempic-type drugs

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:44.840
include nausea, vomiting,
diarrhea, and constipation.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:47.560
And they may also heighten
the risk of pancreatitis,

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:49.440
kidney failure,
and thyroid cancer,

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.120
but for now, let’s stick
to the common ones.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.920
These significant adverse
gastrointestinal effects

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.400
were demonstrated
in virtually all trials,

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.400
though they weren’t bad enough

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.480
to cause more than 15 percent
of trial participants

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.360
to drop out,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.760
and the vast majority
of adverse effects got better

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.680
after they stopped the drugs.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:09.920
Here are the numbers:

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.280
44 percent
experienced nausea,

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:13.800
30 percent diarrhea,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.000
24 percent vomiting,

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.320
24 percent constipation,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.800
and 20 percent
abdominal pain.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.840
But 16 percent of those
on the placebo injections

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.600
experienced nausea
or diarrhea too;

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:25.640
so, it wasn’t all due
to the drug.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.520
People don’t tend to just
spontaneously vomit, though;

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.800
so, that’s more likely
to be a drug-induced effect.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:34.840
So, some people may not
experience side effects at all,

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:37.480
and these GI side effects
have been shown

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.040
likely to be dose-dependent,

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:42.600
and more common during
the dose escalation period.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.480
Thus, it’s recommended
that these medications

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.800
are started at lower doses

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.840
and only increased
as tolerated.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:50.600
So, starting low
and going slow,

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:53.200
gradually nudging up the dose
over many months,

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.480
can minimize
some of these side effects.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.120
And in terms
of what patients can do:

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.640
Eat slowly,
smaller portions.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.360
Eat a low-fat diet.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.840
Small sips of fluid.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.200
Get some fresh air.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.960
Crackers, apples, mint, ginger.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:09.240
Stay hydrated.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.400
Avoid sports drinks,
dairy products,

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:15.040
coffee, alcohol,
and soft drinks.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.040
Temporarily reduce your intake
of fiber or increase it,

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.360
depending on symptoms.

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.000
And if things get really bad,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.740
avoid drinking during meals.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:25.440
If the symptoms persist
or worsen,

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.080
let your healthcare provider
know ASAP.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.480
One thing your doctor can do
is prescribe anti-vomiting drugs

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.360
to counter the side effects
of the original drugs,

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.280
but if you don’t feel nauseated
all the time,

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.360
will you still lose weight?

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.800
Yes, even people who don’t
feel sick to their stomach

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.800
can experience
the appetite suppression

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.840
that leads to weight loss.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.240
GLP-1 also makes you
feel fuller for longer

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.600
by slowing down the rate at
which food leaves your stomach.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.200
That contributes
to the nausea and vomiting,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.320
and can lead
to a serious complication

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:59.360
if you have to go under
anesthesia for surgery.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.080
GLP-1 drugs slow
your stomach down so much

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:05.440
that the American Society
of Anesthesiologists

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:07.200
recommends people
stop taking the drugs

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.920
for up to a week prior
to procedures

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.440
so you don’t go under the knife
with a full stomach,

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.920
for fear that you’ll aspirate
stomach contents

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:16.720
into your lungs.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.480
It turns out that may not
even be long enough.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.680
Patients taking these drugs
had a higher prevalence

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.800
of increased residual
gastric contents despite fasting

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.400
even if they stopped
these drugs a week before.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.120
So, if you’re going in
for elective surgery,

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.920
consider stopping a drug
like Ozempic

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.400
at least three weeks before.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:36.280
Stopping these drugs
for a month or so

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.240
may not be tenable
for diabetics

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:40.000
using it to control
their blood sugars,

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:41.880
but if you’re just doing it
for your weight,

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.760
it’s a good idea to hold off.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.040
GLP-1 type drugs, like Ozempic,

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.160
function by making patients
feel fuller, eat less,

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.480
and hence, lose weight.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.960
However, an important
but often overlooked factor

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:56.680
in these studies
of these kinds of drugs

00:04:56.680 --> 00:04:59.640
relates to the type of weight
that’s lost.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.960
Typically, when people
who are obese lose weight,

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.400
the decrease
in their fat-free mass,

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.080
meaning essentially
their lean mass,

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.560
including their muscles,

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:10.320
usually represents
about 25 percent

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.720
of their total weight loss.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:14.280
So, for every 4 pounds (2 kg)
lost on the scale,

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.080
one of those pounds is not fat.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.360
But on drugs like Ozempic,

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.160
as much as 40 percent
of the total weight lost

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.640
is that lean mass, nearly half
the pounds you’re losing.

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:27.080
Those on Ozempic
or tirzepatide,

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.920
a newer GLP-1 drug
sold as Zepbound,

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:32.480
lost about 14 pounds (6 kg)
of lean mass,

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:35.800
about one eighth of all
the lean mass in their body.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.920
That’s worse than the amount
of lean mass you lose

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.760
when you have
esophageal cancer,

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.080
or head and neck cancer.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.600
Now, some people paid
by the pharma companies

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.360
that make GLP-1-type drugs

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.720
question whether the amount
of muscle mass loss

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.520
is clinically relevant.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:53.480
But these drugs cause
such rapid and significant loss

00:05:53.480 --> 00:05:55.200
of lean mass,
that it’s comparable

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:59.400
to how much you’d lose
over a decade or more of aging.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.560
The drug industry consultants
argue that even if 40 percent

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:04.600
of the weight lost
is lean mass,

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.240
that still means the majority,
60 percent, is fat;

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.440
so, you end up
with a better fat-to-lean ratio,

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:10.800
in the end.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.200
But that’s just
on the first go-around.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.680
Remember, most people
don’t stick to these drugs

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:16.840
for more than a few months,

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:18.240
either because
they can’t keep paying

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:19.560
a thousand bucks a month
for them,

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.760
or they don’t want to put up
with all the side effects,

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:25.480
or deal with drug shortages,
or run out of refills.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:27.680
And when you stop these drugs,

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.560
we know the lost body fat
piles on back,

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.360
but there’s a concern

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.920
that any lost muscle mass
may not;

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:36.960
so, you then actually end up
fatter in the end.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.160
This kind of weight cycling
has been associated

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.160
with extra fat deposition
on the body,

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:42.840
especially around the middle.

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:45.720
Using the gold-standard method,
MRI,

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:48.520
to directly visualize
muscle mass,

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:50.440
researchers found
that the more times

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.080
people cycle their weight,

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:55.080
the worse their body composition
appears to get.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.160
The profound level
of lean mass loss

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.680
associated
with GLP-1 weight-loss drugs

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:01.960
would be expected
to have deleterious impacts

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.320
on health outcomes,
including increased frailty

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.320
and perhaps greater
long-term mortality risk,

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.080
though, this concern
remains theoretical,

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:13.520
since any such long-term data
have yet to be published.

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:16.400
The good news is there’s
something we can do about it.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.760
Exercise, particularly
resistance exercise,

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:19.840
like weight training,

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:22.080
can cut in half or more
the proportion

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:24.440
of fat-free mass that is lost.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.840
Check this out:

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.280
Based on half a dozen studies
of caloric restriction

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:30.440
for weight loss
(like portion control),

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:33.893
and the same calorie restriction
plus resistance exercise,

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:37.880
the non-exercising group
lost more weight.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:39.800
You can guess why, though,

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:41.800
because without
the resistance exercise,

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.680
they lost more lean mass,

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.240
whereas the exercising group
lost nine pounds (4 kg)

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.760
apparently without losing
any lean mass.

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:52.040
Supervised resistance training
interventions,

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:54.440
up to a few times a week
for more than 10 weeks,

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.040
where all major muscle groups
are worked,

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:59.880
can add a few extra pounds
of lean mass.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:02.840
More with weights than cardio,
more when younger,

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:04.880
and more in men than women.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.760
Collectively, this evidence
supports resistance training

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.560
as an effective approach
to, at the very least,

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.040
help mitigate
the decrease in lean mass;

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:16.640
so, programs such as these
should be adopted without delay

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:20.160
in patients embarking
on Ozempic-type therapy.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:22.480
What about "Ozempic face"?

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.440
The term has consumed the media

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.320
with the medication’s
rising popularity

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:28.520
and describes rapid weight loss
in the face

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.880
that leaves
a distorted appearance.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:34.280
And I’d never even heard
of Ozempic butt.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:38.080
Media reports have linked
the drug to facial aging,

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:40.280
but perhaps it’s not so much
the medication

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:42.280
as much as the potent
weight-loss effects

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.880
that leave a sagging appearance

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:46.160
due to the loss of fat
in the face.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:48.320
While this seems logical,

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:50.520
the explanation cannot
fully account

00:08:50.520 --> 00:08:53.120
for the markedly accelerated
facial aging

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.600
seen in GLP-1 drug patients.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.560
The premature facial aging
and altered skin health

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:01.000
appears to be multifactorial,

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:03.360
involving not only the loss
of fat in the face,

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:05.720
but an effect on stem cells
and the production

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:09.280
and secretion of hormonal
and metabolic factors.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:12.280
These changes compromise
the structural integrity

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.160
and barrier function
of the skin

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:18.040
and may lead to diminished
facial muscle mass as well,

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.920
further exacerbating
the appearance of aging.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:24.560
Another side effect of rapid
weight loss is gallstones,

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.040
which is not limited
to GLP-1 drugs.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.880
Shedding
all that excess cholesterol

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.560
stored in your fat cells

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:33.880
can lead to it crystallizing
in your bile like rock candy,

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.840
forming gallstones.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:37.720
Something else to be
cognizant of,

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:38.960
but in a way,

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:41.520
both the muscle loss
and gallstones

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:43.440
may just be signs
of how effective

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.945
these drugs can be
for losing weight.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.120
But as semaglutide’s
popularity soars,

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.280
rare but serious adverse effects
are emerging.

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:55.600
Like, what about possible
thyroid cancer, pancreatitis,

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:58.280
kidney problems, depression,
or suicidal thoughts?

